{
 "_doc": "What a blade meets when it strikes the world (Surfaces, PropHitFX). 'surfaces' is the closed set. A collider carries a 'surface' meta stamped by whoever builds it: kit pieces read 'kits' (a per-kit override) and then 'families' (the material family of the mesh the collider wraps, after any mat_remap); boxes read 'families'; Tripo landmarks and wayside dressing read 'landmarks' (by file name, no extension); scatter reads 'scatter' (by kind); everything else reads 'kinds' (the collider's kind). A collider with no stamp is 'default'. 'none' takes a blow in silence (a soul's body, flame, water). 'ground' is settled at the blow from the footstep surface under the point (AudioDirector.surface_at). 'fx' per surface: particle layers (mesh quad|sliver|chunk; amount; life s; speed [min,max] m/s; gravity m/s2 downward; size [min,max] m; color rgba; spread deg; tex soft|crystal|drip for quads; additive; lit; damping; grow = end scale of a puff; thin = a sliver's width over its length; hot = a brightness factor over 1 for sparks, so they bloom; colours are sRGB), an optional light flash, and the camera shake [trauma, seconds]. The sound is the recorded strike for the surface: AudioDirector.impact(surface, position), audio.json 'impacts'. The sweep itself is tuned in game.json prop_hit.",
